@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Check whether the first administrator has been created
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/setup/status

### Create the first administrator on an unclaimed deployment
### Replace these credentials before sending; never commit real passwords.
### Username: 3–64 letters, digits, underscores, dots or hyphens.
### Password: 12–256 characters. Further claims return 409 already_claimed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/setup/claim
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "REPLACE_USERNAME",
  "password": "REPLACE_WITH_UNIQUE_PASSWORD"
}

### After saving the workspace, bot token, model, and receiver, activate.
### A personal Telegram owner link is optional; an empty membership denies bot use.
@session = REPLACE_SESSION_COOKIE
@csrf = REPLACE_CSRF_TOKEN
@workspaceId = REPLACE_WORKSPACE_UUID
@telegramUserId = REPLACE_TELEGRAM_USER_ID
@requestId = REPLACE_REQUEST_UUID

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/setup/activate
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Get the request link, pending requests, active members, and membership version.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/setup/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/access
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}

### Enroll a known numeric Telegram user ID as an active member.
### Replace version with the value from the preceding GET response.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/setup/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/access
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "actor": "{{telegramUserId}}",
  "version": 1
}

### Or approve a pending request using its ID and the latest membership version.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/setup/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/access-requests/{{requestId}}/decision
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "approved",
  "version": 1
}

### Revoke that member using the latest membership version.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/setup/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/access/{{telegramUserId}}
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 2
}

### Shared provider catalog (operator-owned; API keys are never returned).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/operator/model-providers
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}

### Register a provider and fetch its models. Use the latest catalog version.
### API base URLs without a path use /v1. Saving makes only a /models GET.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/operator/model-providers
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Team API",
  "baseUrl": "https://REPLACE_PROVIDER_HOST/v1",
  "apiKey": "REPLACE_PROVIDER_API_KEY"
}

### Read this workspace's bot model and the shared provider choices.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/models
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}

### Select a model ID returned by the provider, using the current workspace revision.
@providerId = REPLACE_PROVIDER_UUID
@modelId = REPLACE_DISCOVERED_MODEL_ID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/models
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Cookie: repodesk_session={{session}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "revision": 0,
  "selection": {
    "providerId": "{{providerId}}",
    "model": "{{modelId}}",
    "thinkingLevel": "off"
  }
}

### Custom bot models also require modelLimits and modelPricing in selection.
### Codex and Review Bot settings accept the same providerId/model selection in settings.model.
### Codex/Review use a Responses-compatible provider/model; Review can inherit Codex.
